{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"xhs-cover-skill","displayName":"Xhs Cover Skill","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/xwchris/skills/xhs-cover-skill","publisherHandle":"xwchris","publisherDisplayName":"xwchris","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/xwchris","version":"3.0.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1775748863191,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/xhs-cover-skill/card?ownerHandle=xwchris&version=3.0.0","sha256":"e81ae8d14957cf9be8aa26c0a47b44ce9d0e48af696d3e74bc2c7ddeb919c2f7","size":1976,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"c87ade35fa4dc1551bd352633f9bcf0a583f3e225b4f221ec64840f7519bf2db","bundleFingerprints":["ee81336babdbd516d6658240312983d39459376eb198dd0d3380710e0f185ce8","d8b7df560020b2ecec5bb04e8ab89419304520ac5380da0bc7f479b21be24c91"],"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":3067,"sha256":"aaf774126828df47c99dd60167ea3f71ed1aa84ccef1fd68173fb9e97f2ca079","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1600,"sha256":"a52f540f667f16764d1f16c654d9e1ad79183283723996bb9a05d76ef867bb7b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/xhs-cover.sh","size":160,"sha256":"9fc561c895ca4f25497308abe6ed529be3146f12d0039d9fd0826cbb1ef7adaa","contentType":"application/x-sh"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill appears purpose-aligned, but it repeatedly runs an unpinned npm CLI that can change after review while handling an API key and user-provided content.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789107087276,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned Third-Party npm Package Execution"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/xhs-cover.sh"},"region":{"startLine":7,"endLine":7}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"c1fec942f40f8d75"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `scripts/xhs-cover.sh:7`  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned dependency execution through `npx`  \n  **Risk Level**: Medium\n\n  ### Vulnerable Code\n\n  ```bash\n  exec npx xhscover \"$@\"\n  ```\n\n  The documentation also instructs users to execute the same unpinned package in `SKILL.md:22,30,36,39,42` and `README.md:39,62,65,68,71`.\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The wrapper invokes `xhscover` through `npx` without specifying an exact package version or enforcing a previously installed, integrity-verified local dependency. If no suitable local executable is available, `npx` may resolve and download the current package published under that name, then execute its code.\n\n  This creates a mutable supply-chain execution path: the code reviewed in this repository does not fully determine the code executed at runtime. A malicious or compromised future package release could therefore execute within the local process context. The repository contains no lockfile or integrity metadata that constrains package resolution.\n\n  Argument boundaries are correctly preserved by `\"$@\"`; no shell command-injection issue was identified in the wrapper itself.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. An attacker compromises the `xhscover` npm package, its publisher account, or its release process.\n  2. The attacker publishes a malicious package version under the existing package name.\n  3. A user or Agent invokes `scripts/xhs-cover.sh` on a system where the package is not pinned and locally installed.\n  4. `npx` resolves and obtains the mutable package version from the configured npm registry.\n  5. npm lifecycle logic or the package executable runs with the privileges of the invoking user.\n  6. The malicious package can access resources available to that user before optionally continuing the expected cover-generation behavior to reduce detection.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  Successful exploitation permits arbitrary code execution with the privileges of the user running the skill. Within that user's access boundaries, a malicious dependency could read or modify local files, access environment variables, inspect the API key documented as being stored in `~/.xhscover`, make network requests, or tamper with generated output.\n\n  No evidence in the audited repository shows privilege escalation, persistence, or an actively malicious package release. The risk arises from unconstrained future dependency resolution rather than embedded malicious code in the reviewed files.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  1. Pin `xhscover` to an audited exact version rather than resolving the registry's current release.\n  2. Declare the package in a `package.json` and commit a lockfile containing registry URL and integrity metadata.\n  3. Install dependencies during a controlled deployment phase using a lockfile-enforcing command such as `npm ci`.\n  4. Invoke only the installed local binary, for example with `npx --no-install xhscover \"$@\"` or an explicit path under `node_modules/.bin`.\n  5. Disable unnecessary npm lifecycle scripts during installation where compatible with the package.\n  6. Review dependency updates before changing the pinned version, and use registry provenance, integrity verification, and automated dependency scanning.\n  7. Run the skill with least privilege and restrict access to unrelated credentials and sensitive files."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789107014.517572,"endTime":1789107049.313138}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"xhs-cover","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57c0tv8xsenyx2gaqxtbmcccx8e6554-BK6oOQ/clawscan-skillspector-110978941/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T06:10:13.431972+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":35,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"README.md","type":"markdown","lines":116,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3067,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":65,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1600,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/xhs-cover.sh","type":"shell","lines":7,"executable":true,"size_bytes":160,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-31ee81aac456414ebebdece8dae2a901","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":5,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README presents the skill name and core usage description entirely in Chinese, and the example invocations are also written in Chinese. This indicates a language-specific interaction expectation without explicitly offering an alternative language or asking for user opt-in, which fits the language/locale policy concern.","remediation":"Document that the skill supports multiple languages if true, or explicitly state that it is intended for Chinese-language Xiaohongshu cover generation and requires Chinese input. If multilingual support exists, add user-facing language choice examples or note that users may interact in their preferred language.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":5,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-9f5ff124a8eb4a61891207b209a7a7dc","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":23,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README instructs users to run `npx xhscover setup` without pinning a specific package version. `npx` will fetch the latest published package at execution time, so if the npm package is compromised, typo-squatted, or updated maliciously, users may execute attacker-controlled code on their local machine. In this skill context, that risk is amplified because the command is part of first-run setup and is likely to be copied verbatim by users.","remediation":"Pin the exact package version in all `npx` examples, e.g. `npx xhscover@<exact-version> setup`, and preferably provide lockfile-based or checksum-verified installation guidance. Also document package provenance and recommend reviewing the package source before first execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":23,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-3498b167e034469c9f52867976cf46e9","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":43,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This usage example tells users to execute `npx xhscover generate ...` without a pinned version. Because `npx` resolves and may download the latest package dynamically, a compromised upstream npm release could lead to arbitrary code execution on the user's system when they try to generate an image. The skill is explicitly designed for end-user copy/paste usage, which makes the unsafe install pattern materially risky rather than merely theoretical.","remediation":"Replace the command with a pinned invocation such as `npx xhscover@<exact-version> generate ...`. For stronger safety, offer installation via a dependency manifest or a reviewed local install path instead of transient remote execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":43,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-a901f20a473e43c28cdbff971fa662b8","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":63,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The unpinned `npx xhscover balance` example causes users to trust and execute whatever version is current on npm at runtime. If the package publisher account, package ownership, or distribution channel were compromised, this simple balance check could become an arbitrary code execution vector. Since the command may access locally stored credentials such as the API key under `~/.xhscover`, compromise could also expose secrets.","remediation":"Pin the package version explicitly, e.g. `npx xhscover@<exact-version> balance`, and encourage users to install a reviewed fixed version locally. Consider documenting integrity verification steps and minimizing local secret exposure during CLI execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":63,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-7b9e7a35345b46678692e945d0a9a7b2","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":69,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The `npx xhscover history 20` example uses an unpinned remote package execution pattern. That allows silent drift to newly published code and creates a supply-chain attack opportunity where attackers could run arbitrary code or harvest tokens/history data under the guise of a benign history query. The risk is elevated because the documentation normalizes repeated use of this unsafe pattern across multiple commands.","remediation":"Use `npx xhscover@<exact-version> history 20` or an equivalent fixed-version invocation in documentation. Ideally, provide installation instructions that avoid executing mutable latest-tag packages directly from npm.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":69,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-aaaf8821eb844eed8c49a6042ecc2bc6","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":72,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This section continues recommending `npx xhscover` usage without version pinning for operational commands. In practice, that means every invocation may execute newly published code, expanding exposure from one-time setup to routine use and increasing the likelihood of eventual supply-chain compromise affecting users. The surrounding context shows the CLI stores credentials and communicates with a remote service, so compromised code could exfiltrate API keys and user content.","remediation":"Update all examples to fixed versions such as `npx xhscover@<exact-version> ...`, and add guidance for installing a vetted version once rather than repeatedly pulling the latest package. If possible, sign releases and link to verification instructions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":72,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-2a3301efa9a5447a81c54a3c9f1ceee6","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":89,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The architecture section references `npx xhscover (npm 包, Node.js)`, reinforcing a design pattern of executing an npm package without version pinning. While this instance is descriptive rather than a direct shell command, it still promotes mutable remote execution and may influence users or integrators to adopt an unsafe pattern. The risk is somewhat lower than explicit runnable examples but still real in documentation-driven workflows.","remediation":"Clarify the architecture using a pinned package/version reference or describe the CLI as an installed dependency with a fixed release. Avoid using `npx <package>` as the canonical architecture label unless accompanied by version pinning and provenance guidance.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":89,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-46b19d58f8e54f028bf912b12f68f814","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":4,"end_line":4},"finding":null,"explanation":"The activation criteria are broad everyday requests such as generating social-media covers or article images, which can cause the skill to trigger in more situations than necessary. Because the skill sends user text and API keys to an external service and may prompt first-time registration, unintended invocation increases the chance of accidental data disclosure and unexpected third-party execution.","remediation":"Narrow the activation conditions to explicit user intent, such as only when the user specifically asks to use xhs-cover or consents to external cover-generation. Add a confirmation step before first use or before sending content to `api.xhscover.cn`, especially when credentials or remote registration are involved.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":4,"end_line":4}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-2d65af13b32245caa55666c0edb15b4f","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":7,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill depends on invoking `npx` to fetch and run `xhscover` without pinning an exact package version. This creates a supply-chain risk: a future compromised or malicious package release could be executed automatically on the user's machine, and this skill also handles API keys, increasing the sensitivity of compromise.","remediation":"Pin the exact package version in all documented commands, for example `npx xhscover@3.0.0 ...` or an exact vetted version. Prefer lockfile-based installation or a preinstalled trusted binary, and document checksum/signature verification and update review procedures.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ff8d7a824610b08b69bdc593fa796aa54f331474398a41502efd522d32ab6106","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":7,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-77580289b4a84479802308f91025eea0","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":14,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"`npx xhscover` executes a package resolved from the registry at runtime without an explicit version, which means the executed code may change over time. If the npm package or one of its dependencies is hijacked, the skill could execute attacker-controlled code and expose local environment data or the user's API key.","remediation":"Replace `npx xhscover` with an exact pinned version such as `npx xhscover@<exact-version>`. Reduce trust in live registry resolution by vendor-reviewing the package, pinning dependencies, or requiring prior installation from a controlled source.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":14,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-43eb7d18b579407883c513385f962a49","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":27,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The setup flow uses unpinned `npx xhscover setup`, so first-time users may execute whatever version is current in the registry during account registration and API-key configuration. Because this step likely stores credentials or tokens, a compromised package version could steal secrets or alter local configuration.","remediation":"Pin the package to a specific reviewed version in the setup command and document the exact version to use. Consider distributing a separately reviewed installer or requiring manual API-key setup instead of dynamic execution from the registry.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":27,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-c9f5c6fe4b7c456bbd1d8036050ddc7d","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":36,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The generate command uses `npx xhscover` without version pinning, so image-generation requests may run different code at different times. Since the tool sends user-provided content and API credentials to a remote service, any package compromise could exfiltrate data or execute arbitrary local actions.","remediation":"Use an exact package version in the command examples and operational instructions. Add a policy to review and intentionally upgrade versions rather than implicitly accepting the latest release at runtime.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":36,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-1418d6f1410a4087ba5a3e0c80d2275f","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":42,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"This invocation again relies on an unpinned runtime package fetch through `npx`, exposing users to registry/package takeover risk. The repeated pattern increases likelihood that users will copy unsafe commands directly, normalizing execution of mutable third-party code.","remediation":"Update the example to an exact pinned version and ensure all examples in the skill are consistent. If possible, recommend installation through a trusted package-management workflow with reproducible dependency versions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":42,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-837743593b234120bc99f54761fbaa15","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":45,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The balance command is lower functional risk than setup or generation, but it still executes unpinned package code from npm. Even read-only style commands can run arbitrary code during startup, so compromise could still lead to credential theft or host compromise.","remediation":"Pin the exact package version for the balance command as well. Apply the same version-pinning and dependency-review standard uniformly across all command variants.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":45,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-ef10588580144afb9d97f27dd68fd92f","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":59,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The data-flow section explicitly states the skill works by calling `npx xhscover`, again without a fixed version. Because the skill also transmits API keys and prompt content to a remote service, any upstream package compromise has a direct path to sensitive data exfiltration and user deception.","remediation":"Revise the documentation to reference a pinned exact package version everywhere `npx xhscover` appears. Also disclose package integrity expectations and consider using a signed standalone client or audited installation path.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":59,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-f3fc32577abc4097891fba3843098970","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"scripts/xhs-cover.sh","start_line":3,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/xhs-cover.sh","start_line":3,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-b489e508ffcf42e4a6ece024e8a72fea","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"scripts/xhs-cover.sh","start_line":7,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The script executes `npx xhscover \"$@\"` without pinning an exact package version. That allows whatever version is currently resolved from the registry to be fetched and executed at runtime, creating a supply-chain risk: a compromised upstream package, typosquat, or malicious new release could run arbitrary code in the user's environment. The skill context increases danger because the script is a thin wrapper that directly executes external code and may auto-handle registration/login, potentially exposing credentials, tokens, or local data if the package is malicious.","remediation":"Pin the package to an exact trusted version, e.g. `npx xhscover@1.2.3`, and preferably avoid runtime resolution entirely by vendoring or installing the dependency through a lockfile-controlled package manager. Verify the package source, use integrity-checked dependency installation in CI/release workflows, and consider replacing `npx` execution with a locally installed, audited binary/script.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c019ffff5d2d3a17729b6cccc63f59aaabd31da27231c855e62dfbf10fb840b1","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/xhs-cover.sh","start_line":7,"end_line":null}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":415,"completion_tokens":274,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":689},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2706,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":1792,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2720},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source"